The side lengths of the parallelogram can be found from the adjacent vertices.

- Length \(PQ\):
\[
PQ=\sqrt{(2-(-2))^{2}+(1-5)^{2}}
    =\sqrt{4^{2}+(-4)^{2}}
    =\sqrt{16+16}
    =\sqrt{32}=4\sqrt{2}
\]

- Length \(QR\):
\[
QR=\sqrt{(1-2)^{2}+(-2-1)^{2}}
    =\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-3)^{2}}
    =\sqrt{1+9}
    =\sqrt{10}
\]

Opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal, so the perimeter is
\[
2(PQ+QR)=2\bigl(4\sqrt{2}+\sqrt{10}\bigr)=8\sqrt{2}+2\sqrt{10}.
\]

Thus the perimeter of parallelogram \(PQRS\) is  

\[
\boxed{8\sqrt{2}+2\sqrt{10}}.
\]

